---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout page="faq" title="Frequently asked questions | Connectivity Care Solutions" description="Plain-English answers to common questions about the NDIS and working with Connectivity Care Solutions.">
  <section class="faq-section">
    <div class="heart-mark" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 92"><use href="#i-heart"/></svg></div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
      <p class="section-intro">Plain-English answers to common questions about the NDIS and working with us.</p>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq" open>
          <summary><svg class="chev"><use href="#i-chevron"/></svg>What is the NDIS?</summary>
          <div class="body"><p>The National Disability Insurance Scheme (NDIS) is an Australian Government scheme that funds supports for people with permanent and significant disability. It's designed to help people live more independently, pursue their goals and take part in their community.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq">
          <summary><svg class="chev"><use href="#i-chevron"/></svg>Who is eligible for the NDIS?</summary>
          <div class="body">
            <p>In general, to be eligible you need to:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>be under 65 when you apply</li>
              <li>live in Australia and be an Australian citizen, permanent resident or Protected Special Category Visa holder</li>
              <li>have a permanent and significant disability, or be a young child who needs early support</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The NDIS website has an eligibility checklist if you're unsure.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq">
          <summary><svg class="chev"><use href="#i-chevron"/></svg>How do I apply for the NDIS?</summary>
          <div class="body"><p>You can call the NDIS on 1800 800 110 or complete an access request form, along with evidence of your disability from your treating health professionals. If you're not sure where to start, give us a call and we'll talk you through the process.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq">
          <summary><svg class="chev"><use href="#i-chevron"/></svg>What types of support are available?</summary>
          <div class="body"><p>The NDIS can fund a wide range of supports, including help with daily living, getting out in the community, building skills and independence, transport, therapies, assistive technology and home modifications. What's funded depends on your individual needs and goals.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq">
          <summary><svg class="chev"><use href="#i-chevron"/></svg>How is NDIS funding allocated?</summary>
          <div class="body"><p>Funding is based on the supports that are reasonable and necessary for your disability. The NDIA works out a budget from your support needs and goals, and your plan sets out how that funding can be used.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq">
          <summary><svg class="chev"><use href="#i-chevron"/></svg>What is an NDIS plan?</summary>
          <div class="body"><p>Your plan is a document that sets out your goals, the supports you're funded for, how your funding will be managed (by the NDIA, a plan manager or yourself) and when your plan will be reviewed.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq">
          <summary><svg class="chev"><use href="#i-chevron"/></svg>How do I choose an NDIS provider?</summary>
          <div class="body"><p>There are many NDIS providers to choose from. When selecting one, consider their experience, reputation and the services they offer, and whether they're a good fit for you. A registered provider, like Connectivity Care Solutions, meets the NDIS Practice Standards.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq">
          <summary><svg class="chev"><use href="#i-chevron"/></svg>Can I change my NDIS provider?</summary>
          <div class="body"><p>Yes. You have choice and control over who supports you. Check your service agreement for any notice period, then let your current provider know and arrange a start date with your new one.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq">
          <summary><svg class="chev"><use href="#i-chevron"/></svg>What if I need more support than my plan covers?</summary>
          <div class="body"><p>If your needs or circumstances change, you can contact the NDIA to ask for your plan to be changed or reassessed. A support coordinator can help you gather the information you'll need.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq">
          <summary><svg class="chev"><use href="#i-chevron"/></svg>Where can I get more information about the NDIS?</summary>
          <div class="body"><p>Visit <a href="https://www.ndis.gov.au" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ndis.gov.au</a> or call the NDIS on 1800 800 110. You're also welcome to contact us directly with any questions.</p></div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div class="heart-mark" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 92"><use href="#i-heart"/></svg></div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Still have a question?</h2>
      <p>We're happy to talk it through. Call or email us and we'll help you find the answer.</p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href="tel:+61488905457"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-phone"/></svg>Call +61 488 905 457</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="mailto:susan@connectivitycaresolutions.com.au"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-mail"/></svg>Email us</a>
      </div>
      <p style="margin:1.5rem 0 0">Prefer to write it down? <a href="/contact">Send us a message</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
